  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1140 PM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nLittle change in temperature trends expected on Friday however\nmost guidance suggests dewpoints slightly lower. This may be\noptimistic but, at this point, we will take any opportunity for\nslightly lower heat stress conditions. Winds will increase on\nSaturday and higher likelihood of lower dewpoints exists as winds\ntrend west of south allowing drier air to spread eastward. This\nwill raise fire weather concerns especially across E OK including\nthe larger timber fuels of SE OK. \n\nThe anticipated shortwave trough and associated cold front remain\nforecast to pass through the area Sunday through Sunday night.\nIncreasing shower and thunderstorm chances are forecast with the\nfrontal passage and a notable cool down for early next week.\nTemperatures may remain above normal despite the frontal passage\nbut at least triple digit heat will be squashed.",
